# Conspiracy's "As this enchantment enters, choose a creature type" is its own replacement effect (CR 614.1c, 614.12a),
# judged on the permanent as it would exist on the battlefield (CR 614.12): with Opalescence (turn 1) and Humility (turn 3)
# out, Conspiracy would be a creature with no abilities, so on turn 5 nothing is chosen as it enters (the refusal "! Bot1.Modes"
# holds) - it is a 1/1 enchantment creature with no type chosen. On turn 7 Bot1 disenchants Humility: Conspiracy has its
# ability again and is a creature Bot1 controls, but "the chosen type" is none, so it sets no creature type: it has none,
# and is Opalescence's 5/5.

